+# The Flight 93 ground 911 transcript and cassette custody
+
+November 9, 2026 · TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06. Team 7 Box 12 item **412** contains the New York State Police transcription of the ground 911 call made while Glick was speaking with family. Request **35-13 Packet 12** contains an FBI report documenting receipt and copying of two cassettes. These records supply a historical custodian and item-level search keys. They concern the ground 911 line. The possible recording of the incoming Glick call reported in FBI serial **11721** remains a separate lead. [NARA finding aid, Boxes 12–13](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf#page=105) · [Prior recording-account comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/ef5a7cae86a70b59cad5d47a9638fa4526567170/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-flight93-interview-production-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Time fields and sequence
+
+| Record | Field and locator |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Box 12 item 412**, physical pp. 1 and 6 | P. 1 line 9 says **9:20AM** in the evidence description and references **serial 104103**. P. 6 lines 2–4 give **9:20:00** in the transcript heading. The heading identifies a cellular 911 call to the Poughkeepsie tape logger. In the dialogue at p. 6 lines 14–17 and 26–28, the caller says Glick just called and the dispatcher describes him as already speaking with people at the house. |
+| **Same transcript**, p. 44 lines 8–10 | The response to **“The time that the call came in?”** reads **“9:45 roughly.”** This is a transcribed estimate during the exchange. |
+| **FBI 11722** and **April 8 worksheet** | The first interview gives **approximately 9:30 a.m.** for the incoming call, followed by the separate cellular 911 call. The worksheet gives **approximately 9:30** and asks for the ground 911 recording or transcript to establish time. [Prior source locators](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/ef5a7cae86a70b59cad5d47a9638fa4526567170/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-flight93-interview-production-2026-11-09/README.md) |
+| **NPS Flight 93 chronology**, Glick entry | Lists the incoming call at **9:37 EDT**. [NPS chronology](https://www.nps.gov/flni/learn/historyculture/phone-calls-from-flight-93.htm) |
+
+If the printed times refer to those starts on a common clock, the **9:20** heading places the ground call 17 minutes before the published **9:37** incoming call. The opening dialogue gives the reverse order. The **9:45 roughly** estimate supplies a separate time field in the same transcript. This comparison leaves the labels unresolved. A clock offset, incorrect label and differences in event definition are untested possibilities. The original audio, logger channel and clock records, transfer logs and carrier time basis are needed to compare events.
+
+## Custody and production keys
+
+- **Item 412 pp. 1 and 5.** The rendered evidence header gives **FBIITEMNO 302-1A15519**, evidence type **1A**, and refers to **104103**. A September 11 NYSP memo on p. 5 lines 5–17 says logger tapes were removed and secured and gives the tape serial field **13:18:36 9/07/01 - 15:02:37 9/11/01**. At line 16 the embedded layout extraction instead gives **13:18:369/07101 -15:02:379/11/01**. The visual and extracted strings identify their respective layers.
+- **Packet 12 p. 4, stamp 000000811.** The FD-302 says NYSP Troop K, Millbrook, supplied two duplicate cassettes on **September 24, 2001 at 1:24 PM**. Lines 7–10 put the beginning on **Tape A Side A** and the continuation on **Tape B Side A** and state that the call exceeded **45 minutes**. Lines 11–15 report that an agent made two copies of each at **7:10 PM on September 25**, placed all **six cassettes** in a **1A envelope**, and recorded NYSP Troop K Headquarters as retaining the original. The rendered file line shows printed **265A-NY-280350-HQ** with **HQ** struck and handwritten **302-23892**. The extracted line 26 distorts that suffix. The original, master duplicates, four further copies and later disposition remain unlocated. **104103**, **302-23892** and **302-1A15519** occur in different fields. Their complete file-system crosswalk is open.
+- **Packet 12 p. 3, stamp 000000810.** Lines 9–16 report provision of a **43-page** transcript on **September 15**, and earlier provision of selected pages to the New York FBI office and FBIHQ/SIOC on **September 11**. The image prints **pages 1-13** for the earlier selected portion. The embedded text at line 12 gives **pages 1-4.3**. This is a later report of delivery. Original transmission and acknowledgment records remain missing.
+
+## Page accounting
+
+**Item 412** has **48 physical pages** and consecutive visible or embedded page labels **M-NYA-00021775–M-NYA-00021822**. Its first-page header gives **PAGES 93**, **BEGBATES M-NYA-00021775** and **ENDBATES M-NYA-00021867**. The inclusive header range counts 93 labels, with **45** beyond the last label present in this copy. The transcript begins at physical p. **6** and the final page, physical p. **48**, bears internal page **43** and a call-termination line. The 45-label difference concerns the header's larger evidence range. The nature of those additional pages and the reason for the reproduction's extent remain open.
+
+**Packet 12** has **18 physical pages**. Its June 24, 2004 index at p. **2** gives **810** for the September 15 report and **811–825** for the September 24 report with transcript, **16** indexed pages. The copy includes a cover and an index. The visible stamps at pp. **3–5, 9 and 18** give **810, 811, 812, 816 and 825**. Other footer stamps have varying scan degradation. The excerpt comparison ranks item 412 pp. **7–19** first for Packet 12 pp. **6–18** respectively across all 43 transcript pages. Twelve first-place scores lead by over **0.04** in the specified text metric. Packet p. **12** has a margin of **0.000473**, so its specific page match remains tentative. Five selected content checks match. A same-scale translated raster comparison did not reproduce that page mapping. These are content correspondences across scan versions. Which transcript pages were actually transmitted on September 11 and which enclosures belonged to the full evidence range remain open.
+
+## Related staff memo
+
+**Item 413** is labeled **4-2-04** in the ZIP member name. The body, p. 1 line 7, is dated **4/22/2004**. Lines 29–33 record the family recipient disputing the specific World Trade Center threat attributed to her in the earlier interview, while affirming a threat to blow up the plane. The earlier worksheet preserves the attributed target statement at item 267 p. 7 lines 7–10. Keep the accounts and date descriptions separate. The copy supplies the recipient's later reported correction, without audio comparison. [Exact archive member, locators and hashes](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Tests still open
+
+- [ ] **TEL02 / TEL04.** Locate the original logger recording and the FBI cassette envelope and copies, with item inventory and disposition. Match **302-23892**, **104103**, **302-1A15519** and **810–825** through file and exhibit records. Check which recording, transcript and portions were delivered to each recipient and when.
+- [ ] **TEL03 / TEL04.** Recover NYSP logger timing and calibration records and Glick call or relay event records. Test **9:20:00**, **9:45 roughly**, **approximately 9:30** and **9:37 EDT** against the call ordering and source time fields. Preserve the separate **11721** recording inquiry.
+- [ ] **TEL02.** Identify the remaining evidence-range pages and authenticate the reported transmission of the early transcript excerpt.
+
+Two exact public archive members were retrieved and compared with a held Packet 12 reproduction. Twenty PDF field controls and 48 consecutive label checks passed. Thirteen excerpt candidates and five scoped content matches were recorded. Image review used 13 local crops or crop groups covering selected fields. No original audio, network event or calibrated clock was tested. No raw source pages appear in this public supplement. [Source ledger and reproducible comparison scope](SOURCE-PINS.json)
